# Beeline CDN settings

## DNS

- `${BEELINE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}`: `A` -> `${ORIGIN_IP}`
- Optional custom domain: `${BEELINE_CDN_CUSTOM_DOMAIN_DISPLAY}`
- CNAME target when a custom domain is configured: `${BEELINE_CDN_SYSTEM_DOMAIN}`
- Selected Remnawave Host domain: `${BEELINE_HOST_DOMAIN}`

## Origin

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Origin address | `${ORIGIN_IP}:${BEELINE_ORIGIN_PORT}` |
| HTTPS to origin | enabled |
| Origin SNI | `${BEELINE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}` |
| Origin hostname | `${BEELINE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}` |
| Pass original Host | disabled |
| Verify origin certificate | disabled for self-signed bootstrap; enable with a trusted certificate |

## CDN behavior

- Do not cache `${BEELINE_XHTTP_PATH}`.
- Disable secure token, AWS authorization, access restrictions, CORS checks,
  compression/optimization and HTTP/3 for the first test.
- The XHTTP uplink uses GET. A POST response of `405` is expected in the
  provider behavior described by the source guide.

## Checks

```bash
curl -4vk --resolve "${BEELINE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}:443:${ORIGIN_IP}" \
  "https://${BEELINE_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}${BEELINE_XHTTP_PATH}"

curl -vk "https://${BEELINE_CDN_SYSTEM_DOMAIN}${BEELINE_XHTTP_PATH}"
curl -v "https://${BEELINE_HOST_DOMAIN}${BEELINE_XHTTP_PATH}"
```

An HTTP `400` response from the XHTTP endpoint confirms routing to Xray; it is
not a complete protocol session test.
